{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782045842224,"sessionID":"ses_115cd6b79ffeMZxad4uxtd3vMq","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_eb9269b89b444ad18787c62b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs","newString":"pub async fn make_pool(url: &str) -> Result<Pool, sqlx::Error> {\n    let opts = SqliteConnectOptions::from_str(url)?\n        .create_if_missing(true)\n        .foreign_keys(false)\n        .shared_cache(true);\n    // In-memory databases are private per-connection unless shared cache is\n    // used; keep a single connection to guarantee all queries hit the same DB.\n    let max_conn = if url.contains(\":memory:\") { 1 } else { 5 };\n    let pool = SqlitePoolOptions::new()\n        .max_connections(max_conn)\n        .connect_with(opts)\n        .await?;","oldString":"pub async fn make_pool(url: &str) -> Result<Pool, sqlx::Error> {\n    let opts = SqliteConnectOptions::from_str(url)?\n        .create_if_missing(true)\n        .foreign_keys(false)\n        .shared_cache(true);\n    let pool = SqlitePoolOptions::new()\n        .max_connections(5)\n        .connect_with(opts)\n        .await?;"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n@@ -206,10 +206,13 @@\n let opts = SqliteConnectOptions::from_str(url)?\n     .create_if_missing(true)\n     .foreign_keys(false)\n     .shared_cache(true);\n+// In-memory databases are private per-connection unless shared cache is\n+// used; keep a single connection to guarantee all queries hit the same DB.\n+let max_conn = if url.contains(\":memory:\") { 1 } else { 5 };\n let pool = SqlitePoolOptions::new()\n-    .max_connections(5)\n+    .max_connections(max_conn)\n     .connect_with(opts)\n     .await?;\n sqlx::query(\n     \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS books (\\\n","filediff":{"file":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs","patch":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n@@ -206,10 +206,13 @@\n let opts = SqliteConnectOptions::from_str(url)?\n     .create_if_missing(true)\n     .foreign_keys(false)\n     .shared_cache(true);\n+// In-memory databases are private per-connection unless shared cache is\n+// used; keep a single connection to guarantee all queries hit the same DB.\n+let max_conn = if url.contains(\":memory:\") { 1 } else { 5 };\n let pool = SqlitePoolOptions::new()\n-    .max_connections(5)\n+    .max_connections(max_conn)\n     .connect_with(opts)\n     .await?;\n sqlx::query(\n     \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS books (\\\n","additions":4,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"src/lib.rs","time":{"start":1782045842222,"end":1782045842223}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Still 404 on GET /books/{id}. Hmm. The POST returns CREATED and gives an id back, then GET returns 404. So insert happens but the row isn't found afterward. This means the in-memory db is per-connection even with shared_cache? Or maybe shared_cache needs a specific filename.\n\nActually with `:memory:`, each connection creates its own database. To share, you need `file::memory:?cache=shared` URI. Let me change the test url to that. Or better, limit the pool to max_connections(1) for in-memory. Actually simpler: use `max_connections(1)` won't help because INSERT RETURNING should commit.\n\nWait, actually the issue might be autocommit. sqlx uses connections in autocommit mode by default, so INSERT should commit immediately. But if each connection in the pool is a separate in-memory DB, the row goes to one connection's DB and the GET goes to another.\n\nLet me change the test to use `sqlite::memory:?cache=shared` or limit pool to 1 connection. Actually for `sqlite::memory:` URL with shared_cache, sqlx may not handle it. Let me just limit pool to 1 connection for in-memory, OR better: use a temp file in tests.\n\nSimplest: set max_connections(1). But that could be a bottleneck for production. Let me make pool size configurable based on URL, or just use 1 connection always for simplicity. Actually for axum, 1 connection is fine for tests. For production with file DB, multiple is fine.\n\nLet me check: maybe `shared_cache(true)` works with `file::memory:?cache=shared` but not `sqlite::memory:`. The `:memory:` creates a private db. Let me try changing the URL in tests to `sqlite:file:memory:?cache=shared` — but that's awkward.\n\nAlternative: just make the test use a single connection pool. Set `max_connections(1)`. That's fine for tests. For production with a file DB, multiple connections work.\n\nActually, simpler robust approach: detect in-memory and use a single connection. Or always use 1 connection — for a book collection API this is acceptable, but it's a real limitation.\n\nLet me just use a shared in-memory database properly. In SQLite, `file::memory:?cache=shared` works but requires a unique name per process to avoid collisions. Actually you can use `file:memdb1?mode=memory&cache=shared`. \n\nLet me just set max_connections(1) — simpler and works. For a typical embedded use this is fine. Actually let me make it configurable but default to reasonable. For tests with `sqlite::memory:`, 1 connection. For files, 5.\n\nLet me just always use 1 connection to keep it simple — SQLite is single-writer anyway.\n\nActually wait, let me reconsider. The issue is that the pool has 5 connections and `:memory:` creates a separate database per connection. With shared_cache(true) it should share... but maybe sqlx's connection options for `:memory:` don't apply shared_cache.\n\nLet me check: actually, maybe the cleaner fix is to detect `:memory:` and use a single connection. Let me just set max_connections(1) globally. It's simplest and correct.\n\nActually, the cleaner thing: use shared in-memory via a named memory database. Let me update make_pool to rewrite `sqlite::memory:` to use a shared cache file URL.\n\nHmm, let me just go with max_connections(1). It's the pragmatic fix and works for both tests and small deployments.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eea359b28001lgkgtK6KF2Jkyp","sessionID":"ses_115cd6b79ffeMZxad4uxtd3vMq","messageID":"msg_eea35464b0015Me8Ul966lIaP9"}}
