{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782045866566,"sessionID":"ses_115cd6b79ffeMZxad4uxtd3vMq","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_b586fa13c6754babb62a0327","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs","newString":"        .route(\n            \"/books/:id\",\n            get(get_book).put(update_book).delete(delete_book),\n        )","oldString":"        .route(\n            \"/books/{id}\",\n            get(get_book).put(update_book).delete(delete_book),\n        )"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n@@ -232,9 +232,9 @@\n     Router::new()\n         .route(\"/health\", get(health))\n         .route(\"/books\", post(create_book).get(list_books))\n         .route(\n-            \"/books/{id}\",\n+            \"/books/:id\",\n             get(get_book).put(update_book).delete(delete_book),\n         )\n         .with_state(pool)\n }\n","filediff":{"file":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs","patch":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-x571_och/retort-bdffb59492c4/src/lib.rs\n@@ -232,9 +232,9 @@\n     Router::new()\n         .route(\"/health\", get(health))\n         .route(\"/books\", post(create_book).get(list_books))\n         .route(\n-            \"/books/{id}\",\n+            \"/books/:id\",\n             get(get_book).put(update_book).delete(delete_book),\n         )\n         .with_state(pool)\n }\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"src/lib.rs","time":{"start":1782045866563,"end":1782045866564}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Still failing. Even with 1 connection, the GET returns 404. The POST returns CREATED with the body, so the insert worked on connection A. But the GET on the same single connection should find it. Unless... the INSERT isn't being committed?\n\nWait, sqlx uses transactions? No, by default each statement is autocommit. But with `RETURNING` and `fetch_one`, does it leave the transaction open? No.\n\nHmm, but the `list_with_author_filter` test passes — it inserts two books and then lists them and finds them. So inserts DO persist within the same connection. Why does GET by id fail?\n\nLet me look at the test more carefully. The POST returns CREATED, body has `id`. Then GET `/books/{id}` returns 404.\n\nWait — maybe the issue is the route. Let me check the route. `/books/{id}` in axum 0.7... actually axum 0.7 uses `:id` syntax, not `{id}`. The `{id}` syntax is axum 0.8+ or with the `matchit` feature. Let me check axum 0.7.\n\nIn axum 0.7, path params use `:id` like `/books/:id`. The `{id}` syntax was introduced... actually I'm not 100% sure. Let me check. Actually in axum 0.7, the route `/books/{id}` would be treated as a literal path segment `{id}`, not a capture! That's why list (on `/books`) works, but GET/PUT/DELETE on `/books/{id}` doesn't match — returns 404.\n\nWait but POST to `/books` works (create). And GET `/books` (list) works. GET `/books/5` — the route is `/books/{id}` which in axum 0.7 is literal. So `/books/5` doesn't match `/books/{id}` and returns 404. That's the bug!\n\nIn axum 0.7, use `/books/:id`. Let me fix.\n\nActually wait, axum 0.7.9... let me verify. The `{id}` syntax is from axum 0.8 / matchit 0.8. Axum 0.7 uses `:id`. Let me switch to `:id`.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eea35fa3c001xPaw1p2qyM7UoG","sessionID":"ses_115cd6b79ffeMZxad4uxtd3vMq","messageID":"msg_eea35c2da001Pm3haXtbnw6WPF"}}
