{"type":"text","timestamp":1782045916137,"sessionID":"ses_115cd6b79ffeMZxad4uxtd3vMq","part":{"id":"prt_eea36b175001dP8qw0TpRW6nsT","messageID":"msg_eea369d55001mhWicXWlfMMMP5","sessionID":"ses_115cd6b79ffeMZxad4uxtd3vMq","type":"text","text":"Clean build, no clippy warnings, all 5 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented a Rust book-collection REST API using **Axum + SQLx + SQLite**:\n\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — all handlers, DB layer, router, pool setup with auto-created schema. Endpoints: `GET /health`, `POST/GET /books`, `GET/PUT/DELETE /books/:id`. Input validation rejects empty `title`/`author` (400). Proper status codes: 201 on create, 204 on delete, 404 on missing, 400 on bad input.\n- **`src/main.rs`** — binary entrypoint listening on `:3000`, configurable via `DATABASE_URL`.\n- **`tests/api.rs`** — 5 HTTP integration tests (create+get, validation, author filter, update+delete, health) spinning up an in-memory server on an ephemeral port.\n- **`README.md`** — setup/run/test/curl examples.\n\nTwo gotchas caught during the build: axum 0.7 uses `:id` route syntax (not `{id}`), and in-memory SQLite needs a single shared connection to be consistent across queries.","time":{"start":1782045913461,"end":1782045916135}}}
